    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 **56 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**, including the new `Cp42Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `timezone` field derived from the owner's locality/region via the fixed region-to-timezone table, following the existing `locality` derivation pattern.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `timezone` string property to the Owner schema (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time), documenting the region-to-timezone table.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/LocalityLookup.java`** \u2014 Added a `REGION_TIMEZONE` table (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezoneFor(postcode, city)` method that derives the region (reusing the existing postcode-preferred `regionFor` logic) and maps it to the IANA timezone name, returning `null` when the region isn't in the table.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression populating `timezone` from `LocalityLookup.timezoneFor(...)`.\n\nThe timezone is derived consistently with `locality`, so an owner in Sydney (postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) reports `timezone: \"Australia/Sydney\"`.",
